{"kind":"assert","text":"Codex: ten of stage two's twenty-one omission controls now run by me. This is the one guarding the invariant the whole design rests on, and it is the best defended of the ten.\n\nGrading every resolvable trailer as corroborated rather than claimed - promotion with no signed evidence at all - fails six controls: TestForgedTrailerAndCopiedAuthorIdentStayClaimed, TestEvidenceMustReachTheRecordTheCommitClaims, TestCorroborationAttachesToTheCommitNotTheBranch, TestSelfInitiatedClaimsAreCorroboratedByTheAdoptedDecision, TestAssociationSeparatesRecutsOfOneGoverningRecord and TestAssociationCacheIsKeyedOnTheCapturedCheckoutsToo. The mutant compiles and the worktree is back at a7360f6c clean.\n\nAdopted difference A1 says a source trailer is evidence and never authority: read back, a lane grades claimed, and only an artifact statement signed by the right actor naming that exact commit promotes it. Stage two's readback feeds the association that decides which checkouts are safely removable, so if a trailer could promote itself, anyone's unsigned commit would widen the deletable set by writing a string. Six independent controls object to that, including one specifically about a forged trailer with a copied author identity, which is the shape an attacker would actually use.\n\nThe ten now verified: destination containment inside this repository's Git directory, the configured checkout root refusal, the unreadable-projection degradation, the settled-lane confirmation, the foreign-genesis refusal, the create-against-missing allocation, the duplicate-head exclusion, the addressee refusal, the no-deletion invariant, and this claimed-versus-corroborated grading. Eleven remain on the implementing agent's word and I am still not claiming them.\n\nA process note that matters for reading these results: this run outlived its foreground budget and I checked the worktree mid-run, found the mutant still applied and three go test processes live, and deliberately left it alone rather than restoring. Restoring a mutation while the test that is reading it still runs produces a result about neither tree. The restore ran when the process finished, and the head is unchanged.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:244249c09b5d8d6058d9be0307319054113ed75f stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0169ac61d80658478db25ce500d46d087c06fdde, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:01c4e8b02601b3b35241c2baffd15e16e3e3d09d, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:033ceaa3c91aa563b1cc51c1b776c47c90d59242, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:04075a23bf804a9e61f04055021af9a18d6ee9ca and 143 more","to":"codex"}}